# Sandbox-ai Fence v0 — pf anchor rules for the fenced model daemon.
# Loaded into anchor "com.sandboxai/fence" by fence.sh. @FENCE_USER@ is substituted.
#
# Order matters: pf evaluates top to bottom, "quick" stops at the first match.

# Temporary allowances (model downloads). Managed with `fence.sh allow HOST` / `revoke`.
table <sai_allow> persist

# 1. Loopback is always fine: the daemon must serve local apps on 127.0.0.1:11434.
pass out quick on lo0 user @FENCE_USER@
pass in  quick on lo0 user @FENCE_USER@

# 2. Explicitly allowed download hosts, HTTPS only, logged so they appear as receipts.
pass out log quick proto tcp from any to <sai_allow> port 443 user @FENCE_USER@

# 3. Everything else the fenced user sends is dropped and logged. This includes DNS,
#    so the daemon cannot even resolve names: a side door closed by construction.
block out log quick user @FENCE_USER@

# 4. Nothing from other machines may reach the fenced user's sockets. Localhost-only service.
block in  log quick user @FENCE_USER@
